{"id":"mahabharata-8-056","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":56,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 56 · Duryodhana's question about Bhima","summary":{"en":"Seeing the Kauravas broken by Bhima, Duryodhana asks what is to be done, and Karna says that Bhima must be fought together. Satyaki is struck by Karna's arrows, and the dead and wounded fill the field.","kn":"ಭೀಮನಿಂದ ಕೌರವರು ಒಡೆದುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಏನು ಮಾಡಬೇಕೆಂದು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಒಟ್ಟಾಗಿ ಎದುರಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಕರ್ಣ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಣನ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಗಾಯಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಣರಂಗ ಹತ, ಗಾಯಾಳುಗಳಿಂದ ತುಂಬುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"भीम से कौरवों को टूटते देख दुर्योधन पूछता है कि क्या किया जाए, और कर्ण कहता है कि भीम से मिलकर लड़ना होगा। कर्ण के बाणों से सात्यकि घायल होता है और रणभूमि मृतकों और घायलों से भर जाती है।","te":"భీముని చేత కౌరవులు విరిగిపోవడం చూసి ఏం చేయాలని దుర్యోధనుడు అడుగుతాడు; భీమును కలిసి ఎదుర్కోవాలని కర్ణుడు అంటాడు. కర్ణుని బాణాలతో సాత్యకి గాయపడతాడు; రణభూమి హతులు, గాయపడినవారితో నిండుతుంది.","ta":"பீமனால் கௌரவர் உடைவதைக் கண்ட துரியோதனன் என்ன செய்வது என்று கேட்க, பீமனை ஒன்றுசேர்ந்து எதிர்க்க வேண்டும் என்கிறான் கர்ணன். கர்ணனின் அம்புகளால் சாத்யகி காயமுற, களம் இறந்தோராலும் காயமுற்றோராலும் நிறைகிறது.","ml":"ഭീമന്റെ മുന്നിൽ കൗരവർ തകരുന്നത് കണ്ട ദുര്യോധനൻ, ഇനി എന്തു ചെയ്യണമെന്ന് ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമനെ ഒന്നിച്ചു നേരിടണമെന്ന് കർണ്ണൻ പറയുന്നു. കർണ്ണന്റെ അമ്പേറ്റ് സാത്യകി വീഴുന്നു; മരിച്ചവരും മുറിവേറ്റവരും കൊണ്ട് യുദ്ധക്കളം നിറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.56; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो भग्नेषु सैन्येषु भीमसेनेन संयुगे ।\nदुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत्किं नु सौबलो वापि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, when the troops were broken by Bhimasena in the battle, what did Duryodhana do, and what did Shakuni's son do,"}},{"n":2,"text":"कर्णो वा जयतां श्रेष्ठो योधा वा मामका युधि ।\nकृपो वा कृतवर्मा च द्रौणिर्दुःशासनोऽपि वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"or Karna, best of the victorious, or my other warriors in the fight, or Kripa, Kritavarman, Drona's son, or Duhshasana?"}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्यद्भुतमिदं मन्ये पाण्डवेयस्य विक्रमम् ।\nयथाप्रतिज्ञं योधानां राधेयः कृतवानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I find this deed of the Pandava very astonishing, and Radha's son too did as he had vowed with regard to the warriors."}},{"n":4,"text":"कुरूणामपि सर्वेषां कर्णः शत्रुनिषूदनः ।\nशर्म वर्म प्रतिष्ठा च जीविताशा च संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"For all the Kurus, Sanjaya, Karna, slayer of foes, was their shelter, armour, foundation and hope of life."}},{"n":5,"text":"तत्प्रभग्नं बलं दृष्ट्वा कौन्तेयेनामितौजसा ।\nराधेयानामधिरथः कर्णः किमकरोद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that army broken by Kunti's son of boundless might, what did Karna, Adhiratha's son, the Radheya, do in the fight?"}},{"n":6,"text":"पुत्रा वा मम दुर्धर्षा राजानो वा महारथाः ।\nएतन्मे सर्वमाचक्ष्व कुशलो ह्यसि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me all this, Sanjaya, about my unassailable sons and the great chariot-warrior kings, for you are skilled in telling.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"अपराह्णे महाराज सूतपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nजघान सोमकान्सर्वान्भीमसेनस्य पश्यतः ।\nभीमोऽप्यतिबलः सैन्यं धार्तराष्ट्रं व्यपोथयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the afternoon, great king, the glorious charioteer's son killed all the Somakas while Bhimasena looked on, and mighty Bhima in turn broke Dhritarashtra's army."}},{"n":8,"text":"द्राव्यमाणं बलं दृष्ट्वा भीमसेनेन धीमता ।\nयन्तारमब्रवीत्कर्णः पाञ्चालानेव मा वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the army put to flight by wise Bhimasena, Karna said to his charioteer, \"Drive me only against the Panchalas.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"मद्रराजस्ततः शल्यः श्वेतानश्वान्महाजवान् ।\nप्राहिणोच्चेदिपाञ्चालान्करूषांश्च महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shalya, king of the Madras, of great strength, drove his very swift white horses toward the Chedis, Panchalas and Karushas."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रविश्य च स तां सेनां शल्यः परबलार्दनः ।\nन्ययच्छत्तुरगान्हृष्टो यत्र यत्रैच्छदग्रणीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering that army, Shalya, who tormented enemy forces, cheerfully steered the horses wherever the leader wished."}},{"n":11,"text":"तं रथं मेघसंकाशं वैयाघ्रपरिवारणम् ।\nसंदृश्य पाण्डुपाञ्चालास्त्रस्ता आसन्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that chariot, like a cloud, with its tiger-skin cover, the Pandavas and Panchalas were frightened, lord of the people."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो रथस्य निनदः प्रादुरासीन्महारणे ।\nपर्जन्यसमनिर्घोषः पर्वतस्येव दीर्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the rumble of the chariot rose in the great battle, with a sound like thunder or a mountain splitting."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः शरशतैस्तीक्ष्णैः कर्णोऽप्याकर्णनिःसृतैः ।\nजघान पाण्डवबलं शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna too, with hundreds of sharp arrows drawn back to his ear, killed the Pandava forces by the hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":14,"text":"तं तथा समरे कर्म कुर्वाणमतिमानुषम् ।\nपरिवव्रुर्महेष्वासाः पाण्डवानां महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him doing such superhuman work in the battle, the great archers, the Pandavas' great chariot-warriors, surrounded him."}},{"n":15,"text":"तं शिखण्डी च भीमश्च धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च द्रौपदेयाः ससात्यकाः ।\nपरिवव्रुर्जिघांसन्तो राधेयं शरवृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin, Bhima, Dhrishtadyumna the son of Prishata, Nakula, Sahadeva, Draupadi's sons and Satyaki surrounded Radheya, wanting to kill him with showers of arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"सात्यकिस्तु ततः कर्णं विंशत्या निशितैः शरैः ।\nअताडयद्रणे शूरो जत्रुदेशे नरोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki, the brave best of men, struck Karna in the battle on the collarbone with twenty sharp arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"शिखण्डी पञ्चविंशत्या धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पञ्चभिः ।\nद्रौपदेयाश्चतुःषष्ट्या सहदेवश्च सप्तभिः ।\nनकुलश्च शतेनाजौ कर्णं विव्याध सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin struck Karna in the fight with twenty-five arrows, Dhrishtadyumna with five, Draupadi's sons with sixty-four, Sahadeva with seven, and Nakula with a hundred."}},{"n":18,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु राधेयं नवत्या नतपर्वणाम् ।\nविव्याध समरे क्रुद्धो जत्रुदेशे महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And mighty Bhimasena, in anger, pierced Radheya on the collarbone in the battle with ninety well-bent arrows."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः प्रहस्याधिरथिर्विक्षिपन्धनुरुत्तमम् ।\nमुमोच निशितान्बाणान्पीडयन्सुमहाबलः ।\nतान्प्रत्यविध्यद्राधेयः पञ्चभिः पञ्चभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Adhiratha's son, very strong, laughed, shook his fine bow and loosed sharp arrows, afflicting them, and he pierced each of them back with five arrows apiece."}},{"n":20,"text":"सात्यकेस्तु धनुश्छित्त्वा ध्वजं च पुरुषर्षभः ।\nअथैनं नवभिर्बाणैराजघान स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cutting Satyaki's bow and banner, that bull among men struck him between the breasts with nine arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु तं क्रुद्धो विव्याध त्रिंशता शरैः ।\nसारथिं च त्रिभिर्बाणैराजघान परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, tormentor of foes, angrily pierced him with thirty arrows and struck his charioteer with three."}},{"n":22,"text":"विरथान्द्रौपदेयांश्च चकार पुरुषर्षभः ।\nअक्ष्णोर्निमेषमात्रेण तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He left Draupadi's sons without chariots in the blink of an eye, and it seemed a wonder."}},{"n":23,"text":"विमुखीकृत्य तान्सर्वाञ्शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nपाञ्चालानहनच्छूरश्चेदीनां च महारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having turned all of them away with arrows with smooth joints, that brave man killed Panchalas and great chariot-warriors of the Chedis."}},{"n":24,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः समरे चेदिमत्स्या विशां पते ।\nकर्णमेकमभिद्रुत्य शरसंघैः समार्दयन् ।\nताञ्जघान शितैर्बाणैः सूतपुत्रो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down in the battle, the Chedis and Matsyas, lord of the people, rushed at Karna alone and afflicted him with masses of arrows. The great chariot-warrior, the charioteer's son, struck them down with sharp arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतदत्यद्भुतं कर्णे दृष्टवानस्मि भारत ।\nयदेकः समरे शूरान्सूतपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This was a great wonder that I saw in Karna, Bharata: that alone in the battle the glorious charioteer's son"}},{"n":26,"text":"यतमानान्परं शक्त्यायोधयत्तांश्च धन्विनः ।\nपाण्डवेयान्महाराज शरैर्वारितवान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"fought those archers who were striving with all their power, and held back the Pandavas in the battle with his arrows, great king."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्र भारत कर्णस्य लाघवेन महात्मनः ।\nतुतुषुर्देवताः सर्वाः सिद्धाश्च परमर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, Bharata, at the great-souled Karna's quickness, all the gods, siddhas and great sages were pleased."}},{"n":28,"text":"अपूजयन्महेष्वासा धार्तराष्ट्रा नरोत्तमम् ।\nकर्णं रथवरश्रेष्ठं श्रेष्ठं सर्वधनुष्मताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archers, Dhritarashtra's sons, honoured Karna, best of men, the best chariot-warrior and best of all archers."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः कर्णो महाराज ददाह रिपुवाहिनीम् ।\nकक्षमिद्धो यथा वह्निर्निदाघे ज्वलितो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna, great king, burned the enemy's army as a great fire, kindled in summer, burns dry grass."}},{"n":30,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः कर्णेन पाण्डवेयास्ततस्ततः ।\nप्राद्रवन्त रणे भीताः कर्णं दृष्ट्वा महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by Karna here and there, the Pandavas fled in fear in the battle, seeing mighty Karna."}},{"n":31,"text":"तत्राक्रन्दो महानासीत्पाञ्चालानां महारणे ।\nवध्यतां सायकैस्तीक्ष्णैः कर्णचापवरच्युतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a great cry from the Panchalas in that great battle as they were struck by sharp arrows loosed from Karna's fine bow."}},{"n":32,"text":"तेन शब्देन वित्रस्ता पाण्डवानां महाचमूः ।\nकर्णमेकं रणे योधं मेनिरे तत्र शात्रवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Frightened by that sound, the Pandavas' great army thought that Karna alone was the warrior in the battle."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्राद्भुतं परं चक्रे राधेयः शत्रुकर्शनः ।\nयदेकं पाण्डवाः सर्वे न शेकुरभिवीक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya, tormentor of foes, did a wonderful thing there: all the Pandavas together could not even look at him alone."}},{"n":34,"text":"यथौघः पर्वतश्रेष्ठमासाद्याभिप्रदीर्यते ।\nतथा तत्पाण्डवं सैन्यं कर्णमासाद्य दीर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a flood breaks up on reaching the best of mountains, so the Pandava army broke on reaching Karna."}},{"n":35,"text":"कर्णोऽपि समरे राजन्विधूमोऽग्निरिव ज्वलन् ।\nदहंस्तस्थौ महाबाहुः पाण्डवानां महाचमूम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Karna, king, mighty-armed, stood in the battle blazing like a smokeless fire, burning the Pandavas' great army."}},{"n":36,"text":"शिरांसि च महाराज कर्णांश्चञ्चलकुण्डलान् ।\nबाहूंश्च वीरो वीराणां चिच्छेद लघु चेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero swiftly cut off the heads, ears with swinging earrings, and arms of heroes with his arrows."}},{"n":37,"text":"हस्तिदन्तान्त्सरून्खड्गान्ध्वजाञ्शक्तीर्हयान्गजान् ।\nरथांश्च विविधान्राजन्पताका व्यजनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cut into hundreds of pieces elephant tusks, sword hilts, swords, banners, spears, horses, elephants, various chariots, flags and fans, king,"}},{"n":38,"text":"अक्षेषायुगयोक्त्राणि चक्राणि विविधानि च ।\nचिच्छेद शतधा कर्णो योधव्रतमनुष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"axles, shafts, yokes, harnesses and wheels of many kinds, keeping to a warrior's vow."}},{"n":39,"text":"तत्र भारत कर्णेन निहतैर्गजवाजिभिः ।\nअगम्यरूपा पृथिवी मांसशोणितकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Bharata, the earth, with elephants and horses killed by Karna, became impassable, a mud of flesh and blood."}},{"n":40,"text":"विषमं च समं चैव हतैरश्वपदातिभिः ।\nरथैश्च कुञ्जरैश्चैव न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the dead horses, foot soldiers, chariots and elephants, neither rough nor level ground could be told apart."}},{"n":41,"text":"नापि स्वे न परे योधाः प्राज्ञायन्त परस्परम् ।\nघोरे शरान्धकारे तु कर्णास्त्रे च विजृम्भिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither their own nor the enemy warriors could recognise each other in the terrible darkness of arrows, with Karna's weapon spreading."}},{"n":42,"text":"राधेयचापनिर्मुक्तैः शरैः काञ्चनभूषितैः ।\nसंछादिता महाराज यतमाना महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great chariot-warriors who strove were covered with golden-adorned arrows loosed from Radheya's bow."}},{"n":43,"text":"ते पाण्डवेयाः समरे कर्णेन स्म पुनः पुनः ।\nअभज्यन्त महाराज यतमाना महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those Pandava great chariot-warriors who strove in the battle were broken by Karna again and again."}},{"n":44,"text":"मृगसंघान्यथा क्रुद्धः सिंहो द्रावयते वने ।\nकर्णस्तु समरे योधांस्तत्र तत्र महायशाः ।\nकालयामास तत्सैन्यं यथा पशुगणान्वृकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As an angry lion drives herds of deer in the forest, so famous Karna drove warriors here and there in that battle, as a wolf drives herds of animals."}},{"n":45,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवीं सेनां धार्तराष्ट्राः पराङ्मुखीम् ।\nअभिजग्मुर्महेष्वासा रुवन्तो भैरवान्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandava army turned away, Dhritarashtra's sons, the great archers, charged, crying out terrifying shouts."}},{"n":46,"text":"दुर्योधनो हि राजेन्द्र मुदा परमया युतः ।\nवादयामास संहृष्टो नानावाद्यानि सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And King Duryodhana, lord of kings, full of great joy and delighted, had all sorts of instruments played everywhere."}},{"n":47,"text":"पाञ्चालापि महेष्वासा भग्ना भग्ना नरोत्तमाः ।\nन्यवर्तन्त यथा शूरा मृत्युं कृत्वा निवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the great archer Panchalas, best of men, though broken again and again, turned back like heroes who have made death their way back."}},{"n":48,"text":"तान्निवृत्तान्रणे शूरान्राधेयः शत्रुतापनः ।\nअनेकशो महाराज बभञ्ज पुरुषर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya, tormentor of foes, bull among men, broke those heroes as they turned back, many times, great king."}},{"n":49,"text":"तत्र भारत कर्णेन पाञ्चाला विंशती रथाः ।\nनिहताः सादयः क्रोधाच्चेदयश्च परःशताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, Bharata, Karna killed twenty Panchala chariot-warriors with their attendants, in anger, and more than a hundred Chedis."}},{"n":50,"text":"कृत्वा शून्यान्रथोपस्थान्वाजिपृष्ठांश्च भारत ।\nनिर्मनुष्यान्गजस्कन्धान्पादातांश्चैव विद्रुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having emptied chariot seats, horses' backs and elephants' necks of men, and put the foot soldiers to flight, Bharata,"}},{"n":51,"text":"आदित्य इव मध्याह्ने दुर्निरीक्ष्यः परंतपः ।\nकालान्तकवपुः क्रूरः सूतपुत्रश्चचार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"the cruel charioteer's son, tormentor of foes, moved about, hard to look at like the midday sun, with a form like Death the ender of ages."}},{"n":52,"text":"एवमेतान्महाराज नरवाजिरथद्विपान् ।\nहत्वा तस्थौ महेष्वासः कर्णोऽरिगणसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed those men, horses, chariots and elephants, great king, that great archer Karna, destroyer of enemy hosts, stood there."}},{"n":53,"text":"यथा भूतगणान्हत्वा कालस्तिष्ठेन्महाबलः ।\nतथा स सोमकान्हत्वा तस्थावेको महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As mighty Time stands having killed hosts of beings, so that single great chariot-warrior stood, having killed the Somakas."}},{"n":54,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम पाञ्चालानां पराक्रमम् ।\nवध्यमानापि कर्णेन नाजहू रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here we saw a wonder in the valour of the Panchalas: though struck by Karna, they did not give up the fight at the head of the battle."}},{"n":55,"text":"राजा दुःशासनश्चैव कृपः शारद्वतस्तथा ।\nअश्वत्थामा कृतवर्मा शकुनिश्चापि सौबलः ।\nन्यहनन्पाण्डवीं सेनां शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Duhshasana, Kripa son of Sharadvat, Ashvatthama, Kritavarman and Shakuni son of Subala killed the Pandava army by the hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":56,"text":"कर्णपुत्रौ च राजेन्द्र भ्रातरौ सत्यविक्रमौ ।\nअनाशयेतां बलिनः पाञ्चालान्वै ततस्ततः ।\nतत्र युद्धं तदा ह्यासीत्क्रूरं विशसनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Karna's two sons, brothers of true valour, king of kings, strong, destroyed the Panchalas here and there. Then the fighting was cruel and a great slaughter."}},{"n":57,"text":"तथैव पाण्डवाः शूरा धृष्टद्युम्नशिखण्डिनौ ।\nद्रौपदेयाश्च संक्रुद्धा अभ्यघ्नंस्तावकं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way the brave Pandavas, Dhrishtadyumna, Shikhandin and Draupadi's sons, in anger struck down your army."}},{"n":58,"text":"एवमेष क्षयो वृत्तः पाण्डवानां ततस्ततः ।\nतावकानामपि रणे भीमं प्राप्य महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So this destruction came upon the Pandavas here and there, and on your men too, in the battle, when they met mighty Bhima.\""}}]}]}